The block-operator and optimized-value adaptations replace the upstream
two-block decomposition by arbitrary finite dependent block families. They
also revise imports and namespaces and add the matrix/spectral-entropy
interfaces needed here. OptimizedBridgeBase.lean and OptimizedBridge.lean
provide the conversion to entropy in bits and the literal sInf definition.
StrictLogOrder.lean narrows imports and changes the namespace; its cited
mathematical proofs are unchanged.

Capacity/WeakReduction.lean adapts the finite-ensemble mixing and pure-to-mixed
argument to preserve one output logarithmic expectation. Capacity/GibbsMatrix.lean
adapts the scalar-line derivative argument to prove the entropy tangent bound.
The generic standard entropic criterion in UpperBound.lean is imported directly
from the pinned dependency; the local StandardCriterion.lean proves its exact
conversion to the manuscript's entropy convention in bits.

The Qubit/OutputForm, ChannelBoundAlgebra, ChannelBound, and EnsembleEntropy
adaptations replace the two-dimensional input space by an arbitrary finite
input space. The local scalar ensemble construction and block-entropy bridge
discharge the required entropy estimates. DecompositionAlgebra and
DecompositionRotation generalize the row Gram and polynomial rotation
arguments to arbitrary input dimension. PSDFactor generalizes the positive
Schur-complement and compactness construction to an arbitrary fixed number
of common Kraus columns. The exact channel additivity results are assembled
locally from these ingredients and this repository's block entropy theorem.

PhaseCovariant/NoiseEntropy.lean generalizes the normalization and Jensen
argument from Partner.lean to arbitrary nonnegative masses and density
matrices, including zero total mass. The phase-covariant channel theorem is
assembled locally from the proved normal form, finite symmetry averaging,
this repository's block entropy theorem, and the weaker entropic criterion.

DecompositionRotation.lean also follows the determinant coefficient proof
pattern in Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Polynomial.lean, mathlib commit
5ed2965256430c3649e86755f9576b54eca72435, licensed under Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4

